From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Velez Garcia <velezgarciaemmanuel25@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 19:02:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Extended knockback models and PvP tuning

Ports the option set competitive 1.8 forks expose, so knockback can be
tuned to taste instead of only scaling vanilla's numbers.

knockback.type picks between three models:
  SIMPLE   - vanilla's, plus 1.7 style reduced knockback on back hits so
             chasing a fleeing player is possible again
  ADVANCED - separate horizontal/vertical friction with modifiers for
             on-ground, in-air and sprinting states, a fixed back-hit
             value, an optional vertical cap and a Knockback enchantment
             deduction
  CONSTANT - discards the victim's motion entirely so every hit travels
             the same distance, with separate values for sprint-reset
             hits and for victims already airborne

Also adds combo mode, arrow knockback with bow boosting, a fishing rod
speed multiplier, configurable splash potion throwing, a separate
invulnerability window for arrows, and an optional attacks-per-second cap.

All defaults reproduce the previous behaviour.

